<p>Use the following procedure to have the image printed rotated by 180 
 degrees.</p>
<p>For example, use this function if paper loaded in a tray has the top 
 and bottom fixed, and printing with the paper in that direction would 
 otherwise make the image upside-down.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> menu 
 on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Rotate by 180 
 Degrees</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
